// Title: Change the Fax Dll
// Sigma ID: 9e3357ba-09d4-4fbd-a7c5-ad6386314513
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-07-17 | Modified: 2022-12-30
// ATT&CK: persistence, defense-impairment, T1112
// Description: Detect possible persistence using Fax DLL load when service restart
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/dottor_morte/status/1544652325570191361
//   - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/RiccardoAncarani/talks/master/F-Secure/unorthodox-lateral-movement.pdf
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_fax_dll_persistance.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Software\\Microsoft\\Fax\\Device Providers.*$" and RegistryKey contains "\\ImageName") and (not(RegistryValueData =~ "%systemroot%\\system32\\fxst30.dll"))
